---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/pages.css';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Carbon Impact Studies | Site-Wide Carbon Masterplanning | Rubix MEP"
  description="Site-wide carbon impact studies from Rubix MEP: dynamic modelling that quantifies carbon emissions, energy use and operational costs, establishing a pragmatic route to net zero."
  ctaSub="One building or a whole estate. Start with the numbers."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="bg" role="img" aria-label="City skyline blended with forest treeline in Rubix navy duotone"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow rv"><span class="dot"></span>Our differentiator</div>
      <h1 class="disp rv rv-d1">Site-wide <span class="c-green">carbon</span> impact studies</h1>
      <p class="lede rv rv-d2">Early-stage masterplanning for new or existing sites that establishes a potential route to net zero <span class="c-green">carbon</span> operation, through dynamic modelling simulations. Decisions informed by numbers, not assumptions.</p>
      <div class="ctas rv rv-d3" style="margin-top:30px; display:flex; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-lime">Discuss your site <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
        <a href="/projects/national-trust-carbon-impact-studies" class="btn btn-ghost">See it in practice</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT A STUDY DELIVERS -->
  <section class="sec-pad">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="outputs">
        <div class="rv shead2">
          <div class="ndash"></div>
          <h2><span class="c-green">Carbon</span> reduction &amp; energy use impact studies</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--grey); margin-top:14px; line-height:1.75;">A <span class="c-green">carbon</span> impact study enables clients to evaluate the <span class="c-green">carbon</span> emissions impact, energy use and operational costs of a given site, so long-term <span class="c-green">carbon</span> reduction masterplanning can be carried out in a pragmatic manner. Typical outputs include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Assessment of entire sites to establish opportunities for site-wide <span class="c-green">carbon</span> and energy use reduction</li>
            <li>Review and evaluation of associated capital and ongoing operational costs, with potential Return on Investment (ROI) calculations</li>
            <li>Electric Vehicle (EV) charging site-wide impact, informing the wider electrical infrastructure assessment</li>
            <li>Evaluation of potential locations for optimal PV installations and associated yield calculations</li>
            <li>Visual representation of existing building stock characteristics to inform priority works</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="chart-card rv rv-d1">
          <img src="/assets/carbon-4-step-chart.jpg" alt="Four-step carbon reduction chart: stepped reductions from current emissions towards minimum operational carbon" />
          <div class="cap">The four-step approach: from establishing the current baseline to a defined route to minimum operational <span class="c-green">carbon</span>.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE FOUR STEPS -->
  <section class="sec-pad soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead2 rv">
        <div class="ndash"></div>
        <h2>A pragmatic, <b>four-step approach</b></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step rv">
          <div class="n">1</div>
          <h3>Baseline the site</h3>
          <p>Survey the existing building stock and services infrastructure; model current energy use and <span class="c-green">carbon</span> emissions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step rv rv-d1">
          <div class="n">2</div>
          <h3>Model the scenarios</h3>
          <p>Dynamic simulation of future scenarios: passive measures, energy efficiency improvements and renewable / LZC technologies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step rv rv-d2">
          <div class="n">3</div>
          <h3>Evaluate the economics</h3>
          <p>Capital and operational costs, ROI and payback calculations for each option, rationalised into site-specific recommendations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step rv rv-d3">
          <div class="n">4</div>
          <h3>Define the route</h3>
          <p>A clear, prioritised masterplan towards minimum operational <span class="c-green">carbon</span>, aligned to your targets and budget cycles.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROOF -->
  <section class="proof-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="kick rv">Proven at estate scale</span>
      <h2 class="rv rv-d1">First-of-its-kind for the National Trust, now rolling out UK-wide</h2>
      <p class="rv rv-d2">Our Coleton Fishacre study was the first detailed energy and <span class="c-green">carbon</span> analysis model of its kind for the National Trust, supporting their pledge of net zero <span class="c-green">carbon</span> by 2030 and a minimum 5% annual reduction in Scope 1 and 2 CO<sub>2</sub> emissions. Further studies are now planned and underway across multiple Trust sites.</p>
      <div class="q rv rv-d2">&ldquo;The study enabled the National Trust to evaluate the <span class="c-green">carbon</span> emissions impact, and associated energy use and operational costs, of a given site post refurbishment.&rdquo;</div>
      <div class="by rv rv-d3">National Trust <span class="c-green">carbon</span> impact study, Coleton Fishacre</div>
      <div class="ctas rv rv-d3" style="margin-top:32px;">
        <a href="/projects/national-trust-carbon-impact-studies" class="btn btn-lime">Read the case study <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
